                <td><a href="/p/@Model.Dataset/checks?check=notnames"><strong>Entities that are not names</strong></a></td>
                <td class="small">Entities made for "s.n.", "S.l.", "[publisher not identified]" or a stray letter: the cataloguer's way of saying nothing is known, or a slip. Each is decided as not a name and removed.</td>
                <td><strong>@Model.NotNames.Count.ToString("N0")</strong> entit@(Model.NotNames.Count == 1 ? "y" : "ies")<br /><span class="small muted">on @Model.NotNames.Sum(n => n.Records).ToString("N0") records</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><a href="/p/@Model.Dataset/checks?check=thin"><strong>Places that say too little</strong></a></td>
                <td class="small">Places with no gazetteer's or Wikidata's identifier, so nothing says where they are: they stand low on a card and are missing from its map. Each is given the gazetteer's record of it.</td>
                <td><strong>@Model.Thin.Count.ToString("N0")</strong> place@(Model.Thin.Count == 1 ? "" : "s")<br /><span class="small muted">@Model.Thin.Count(p => p.Offer is not null && p.Holder is null) with one record to give</span></td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
}
}
